Adapted material:

  - src-tauri/detect/claude.toml and src-tauri/detect/codex.toml are derived
    from Herdr's agent detection manifests (src/detect/manifests/claude.toml
    and codex.toml). Modified: schema simplified for Pitwall's rule engine,
    regions narrowed, rules added and removed (see file headers).
  - src-tauri/detect/gemini.toml, opencode.toml, cursor.toml, copilot.toml,
    qwen.toml and amp.toml are derived from Herdr's manifests of the same
    agents (src/detect/manifests/gemini.toml, opencode.toml, cursor.toml,
    github-copilot.toml, qwen.toml and amp.toml). Modified: schema
    simplified, whole-screen regions narrowed to the bottom of the screen,
    the OSC progress rule dropped, detail hints and an explicit idle
    fallback (Herdr's engine default for known agents) added. The tests in
    src-tauri/src/detect/tests_more_agents.rs use screens built from the
    UI strings in those manifests.
  - The resume flags in src-tauri/agents/opencode.toml, copilot.toml and
    qwen.toml follow Herdr's src/agent_resume.rs.
  - The rule model in src-tauri/src/detect.rs (priority-ordered rules over
    screen regions with contains/regex/line_regex and all/any/not gates, and
    the region helpers such as the prompt box and the Codex prompt marker)
    follows the design of Herdr's src/detect/manifest.rs.

